4. Why Are We Separating Schemas?
************************************

Imagine everything is in one schema:

dbo
│
├── sales
├── customers
├── dim_customer
├── fact_sales
├── sales_dashboard
├── cleaned_sales
├── raw_sales
└── ...

Very quickly it becomes difficult to understand:

Which table is raw?
Which table is cleaned?
Which table should Tableau use?

Schemas give us organization.

bronze → Raw
silver → Clean
gold   → Analytical Model
mart   → Business Consumption

