9. Your First Query

Run:
SELECT *
FROM bronze.sales;
| order_id | customer_id | product_id | store_id | quantity | unit_price | discount |
| -------: | ----------: | ---------: | -------: | -------: | ---------: | -------: |
|     1001 |         501 |        101 |       10 |        2 |        500 |       50 |
|     1001 |         501 |        102 |       10 |        1 |        800 |        0 |
|     1002 |         502 |        101 |       11 |        3 |        500 |      100 |
|     1003 |         501 |        103 |       10 |        1 |       1200 |      200 |
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
🔥 Notice the Grain

Look at:

order_id = 1001

It appears twice.

Why?

Order 1001
│
├── Product 101
└── Product 102

Therefore:

One row = one product line within an order.

This is your fact_sales grain.

This is exactly the concept we fixed before starting Phase 1.
